            "items": [
                {
                    "id": 1,
                    "img": "images/pictures/about-texts-image-1.png",
                    "faIcon": "",
                    "faIconColors": {"bg": "", "fill": ""},
                    "locales": {
                        "en": {
                            "text": "<p>My early years were shaped by frequent relocations due to my father's government service. This journey allowed me to study in multiple schools across different regions, enriching my perspective and adaptability.</p><p>After completing my college education at Notre Dame College, I earned a place at BUET, where I am currently pursuing my undergraduate studies. My passion for engineering and innovation has led me to become actively involved in BUET Automobile Club and Team Interplanetar, the university's Mars Rover team. These experiences have not only honed my technical skills but also strengthened my ability to collaborate and lead in dynamic team environments.</p><p>Currently, I am in Level 2, Term 1 of my undergraduate studies at BUET. Alongside my academic coursework, I am actively involved in BUET's Mars Rover project as a member of Team Interplanetar. I am also a part of the BUET Automobile Club, where I engage in projects that align with my passion for engineering and innovation. Beyond academics, I have a strong interest in cinematography and photography, which add a creative dimension to my work. Additionally, I actively participate in various extracurricular activities at my university, further developing my leadership and teamwork skills.</p>"
                        }
                    }
                }
            ]
        },

